            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "chassis_status_monitor.cpp",
                    "line": 179,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "worth combining into 1 line?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_status_monitor.cpp",
                    "line": 179,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Will do."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_status_monitor.cpp",
                    "line": 179,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_status_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Since this and pgood were only an int due to legacy reasons, would it be good here to just have it be a normal bool so others don't have to care about the int?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_status_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "I thought about this. The complicating factor is that there are applications outside of the phosphor-power repository that use those two D-Bus properties.\n\nIt is also possible that a third or fourth state could be defined at some point, like PoweringOff/PoweringOn.\n\nFor that reason, I decided to keep it the same for now to avoid scope creep. It could be changed later as a separate effort."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_status_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "I do define constants for the integer values in the subsequent commit https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-power/+/86320.\n\nSo users of this property can compare to ON and OFF vs. hardcoding that 1 == ON."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 179,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "these are almost in alphabetical order..."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 179,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Are you referring to the generated error_*pp files? I hadn't moved them since the name is a variable."
                }
            ],
